      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The \"enforcement-first\" view is a fundamentally reactionary stance that prioritizes control over constructive growth. A nation's long-term stability is built on a robust economy and a functioning society, both of which require a diverse, integrated workforce. Rewarding legal compliance through citizenship is not rewarding lawbreaking; it is incentivizing adherence to the rule of law by offering a tangible benefit for following the established process.",
      "source": "target",
